<title>JAPAN: Australia's EFIC launches 6.09% yen/NZ$ samurai.</title>
<headline>Australia's EFIC launches 6.09% yen/NZ$ samurai.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/New Zealand dollar dual currency samurai bond issue was announced by lead manager Kokusai Securities on Tuesday.</p>
<p> BORROWER	  Export Finance and Insurance Corp (EFIC)</p>
<p> AMT		 10 billion yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    6.09 pct</p>
<p> MATURITY	  28 Jan 1999</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  28 Jan 1997</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Semi-annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P AA</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Kokusai Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Fuji Bank</p>
<p>NOTES: The bonds guaranteed by the government of Australia. Holders of the samurai bonds will receive NZ$6,101.28 for each 500,000-yen bond held at maturity.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8785</p>
</text>
